			<div1 type="documentation">
				<div2>
					<head>Introduction</head>
					<div3>
						<!-- Provide link to the Annotation Guidelines once published online. -->
						<head>About LADaS</head>
						<p>LADaS, which stands for "Layout Analysis Dataset with SegmOnto," is both a controlled
							vocabulary and a dataset. It was originally created as part of the <ref
								target="https://colaf.huma-num.fr/en/">COLaF Project</ref> (INRIA), before being
							extended to the <ref target="https://atrium-research.eu/">ATRIUM Project</ref>.</p>
						<p>As a controlled vocabulary, LADaS aims at describing the layout of printed or
							typewritten textual documents, and their related materials (e.g. posters,
							manuscripts). It is derived from the preexisting <ref
								target="https://segmonto.github.io/">SegmOnto controlled vocabulary</ref>, but
							provides a more detailed description of the page layout by focusing on the graphical
							representation of elements like paragraphs, headings, tbales, forms, or images.</p>
						<p>The core of the LADaS model is to be able to reconstruct a document from its image
							into a TEI file.</p>
					</div3>
					<div3>
						<head>About this Document</head>
						<p>This document presents the TEI customisation for LADaS-generated files. It provides
							explanations for the mapping between the LADaS layout annotations for zone
							segmentation and the TEI standard as described in the <ref
								target="https://tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/index.html">
								Guidelines</ref>.</p>
						<p>Due to the inherent nature of LADaS, modules like "namesdates," through crucial for
							the encoding of digital scholarly editions, are not included because they go beyond
							the reconstruction of a document's layout.</p>
					</div3>
				</div2>

